<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashina Helu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 659</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashina-clan">Ashina</a> Helu was the last independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-turkic-khaganate">Western Turkic Khaganate</a>. Once a Tang <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, he rebelled in 651 and reunited the Western Turks, but in 657 a Tang army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/su-dingfang">Su Dingfang</a> defeated him near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irtysh">Irtysh River</a>. Captured and taken to the Tang capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>, he was pardoned by Emperor Gaozong and died there in 659. The Tang then ruled the western steppe through puppet khagans.</p></div>
